    "background_story": "April grew up in a family of skilled craftsmen and women, but she never felt a connection to the traditional trades. That was until she stumbled upon an old gunsmithing workshop in her small town. The owner, a grizzled veteran named Joe, took her under his wing and taught her the intricacies of firearms design and repair. April's natural talent and attention to detail quickly made her a skilled gunsmith in her own right. She opened her own shop, where she specialized in custom rifle builds and historical reproductions. Her work was highly sought after by collectors and hunters alike, and she became known for her meticulous craftsmanship and innovative designs. April's passion for gunsmithing had not only given her a sense of purpose but also allowed her to preserve a traditional craft for future generations.",
